# Data licenses and attribution

Scenic Drive is built on open data. The scenic index, routing graph and basemap tiles are derived works of the
sources below and are distributed under the terms those sources require.

## OpenStreetMap — ODbL 1.0
© OpenStreetMap contributors. Data available under the Open Database License, https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright.
Our derived databases (the scenic segment corpus, the tagged routing extract, the basemap tiles) contain information
from OpenStreetMap and are themselves offered under the ODbL. The scoring algorithm and its weights are ours.
Attribution "© OpenStreetMap contributors" is shown on every map surface in the app.

## Protomaps basemap tiles
Built from OpenStreetMap with Protomaps (https://protomaps.com), attributed as "© OpenStreetMap contributors · Protomaps".

## Places
- Foursquare OS Places — Apache License 2.0. https://opensource.foursquare.com/os-places/
- Overture Maps Foundation Places — CDLA-Permissive-2.0 (OSM-derived rows ODbL). https://overturemaps.org

## United States government data — public domain (17 U.S.C. § 105)
- USGS 3D Elevation Program (3DEP) 1/3 arc-second DEM
- USFS / MRLC Tree Canopy Cover; MRLC Annual NLCD fractional impervious surface
- FHWA America's Byways (HEPGIS Scenic_Byways)
- FCC Broadband Data Collection mobile coverage
- NPS API, Recreation.gov RIDB

## State of California
- Caltrans Scenic Highway System GIS layer; Caltrans Lane Closure System (LCS)
- 511 SF Bay Traffic Events (MTC), used under its open data terms

## Wikimedia Commons
Geocoded photo *counts* are used as a signal. No images are redistributed.

## Solar computation
NOAA Solar Calculator equations (public domain), computed on device.
